from northern, central, and southwestern Madagascar (Fig. 42): Antsiranana Prov.; Toliara Prov.; Fianarantsoa Prov.","","text","",""]]},"NP2SZ":{"d":[["Distribution. Diastatotropis elegans is so far known only from northern Madagascar, from Montagne d’Ambre National Park. All historical specimens labelled with exact locality data come only from this area. The specimens labelled as ‘ Diego Suarez’ in BMNH undoubtedly come from Montagne d’Ambre, since this city, known today as Antsiranana, is located in its immediate vicinity. Also, the senior author (MT) found this species exclusively in Montagne d’Ambre National Park during his 11 expeditions focused on collecting Malagasy anthribids. Thus, we cautiously consider D. elegans to be endemic to the Montagne d’Ambre area.","","text","",""]]},"NXLK":{"d":[["","CN","iso","native",""]]},"PCTNH":{"d":[["European Marine Waters","7130","mrgid","native",""],["North East Atlantic","5664","mrgid","native",""]]},"PZBQ":{"d":[["CALOO","","text","native",""]]},"Q3X3N":{"d":[["CD, North Kivu","","text","native",""]]},"Q86HV":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"Q9BQ":{"d":[["New Zealand","","text","",""]]},"QLKB3":{"d":[["Distribution. Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya.","","text","",""]]},"QWTN3":{"d":[["Oaxaca","","text","",""]]},"QZ5CZ":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","",""]]},"R48M2":{"d":[["Ethiopia","","text","",""]]},"R4ZGV":{"d":[["Australia","","text","",""]]},"R6Q4P":{"d":[["Distribution. Philippines.","","text","",""]]},"RC2KK":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""],["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"RPPK":{"d":[["Australasia","","text","native",""]]},"RTWLT":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"RV3P2":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"S8LT2":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"SFBB":{"d":[["","CAL-OO","tdwg","native",""],["USA (CA)","","text","native",""]]},"SMSJ":{"d":[["European waters (ERMS scope)","7130","mrgid","",""],["North Atlantic","1912","mrgid","",""],["North West Atlantic","7135","mrgid",""